{#
  A standalone FAQ URL, separate from the accordion on the About page.

  Worth its own page because a question-and-answer pair is already the shape an
  AI system is looking for when it answers a question about a person. The
  FAQPage schema is emitted here only — duplicating it on About as well would
  put two competing FAQPage objects on one site.
#}
<section class="page-head wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--blue)">FAQ</p>
  <h1 class="display">The short answers.</h1>
  <p class="prose measure">Direct answers to what people usually ask. If yours isn&rsquo;t here, <a href="/contact/">ask me</a>.</p>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight wrap" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="faq">
    {%- for item in faq %}
    <details{% if loop.first %} open{% endif %}>
      <summary>{{ item.q }}</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">{{ item.a }}</div>
    </details>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="measure prose" style="margin-top:3rem">
    <h2 class="headline" style="font-size:1.5rem">Verify</h2>
    <p>If you&rsquo;re confirming you have the right Max Murphy, the
      <a href="/who-is-max-murphy/">disambiguation page</a> lists every profile I maintain.
      Machine-readable versions of this information are at
      <a href="/resume.json">resume.json</a> and <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band cta">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="headline">Didn&rsquo;t answer it?</h2>
    <p style="margin-top:2rem">
      <a class="btn btn--solid" href="/contact/" style="background:#fff;color:var(--blue)">Get in touch</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
